PRIOR RESEARCH
[{'question': 'What recurring real-tender failure classes and bounded directions should inform the next hypothesis?', 'findings': 'The intact corpus reconstructs the 130 review rows (253 total minus 90 labelled minus 33 provisional NOT_FOUND); the supplied review-pool gzip remains CRC-corrupt. The largest viable-looking unresolved class is branded threaded ball valves: 53 ball-valve rows, 42 with third-party brands, including 30 IVR rows. Current canonicalization emits an alternate for only 40/130 review rows, and none for representative IVR/VALTEC rows. Official manufacturer data shows the opaque IVR 954/956 codes carry material retrieval facts: full-bore threaded ball valve and F/F versus M/F endpoints; VALTEC VT.214 likewise identifies a ball valve with an internal-thread endpoint. LD has hundreds of brass threaded ball-valve products, including explicit В-В/В-Н and handle variants, so this is a real vocabulary/underspecification gap—not evidence that foreign branded products are automatically interchangeable with LD.\n\nA separate correctness defect is confirmed: the clause terminator treats the embedded «ШТ.» in a technical designation as a quantity token, reducing «Кран БИВАЛ КШТ.11.050.025.ф/ф 50х25 КОФ» to «Кран БИВАЛ К». This should be repaired by token-boundary parsing, not a designation-specific rule. The pool also contains 33 filter/water-treatment rows and explicit work rows; many are consumables or service requests, but a few service lines embed a product, so broad abstention is unsafe.\n\nPromising directions: (1) a bounded, fail-open runtime manufacturer/model enrichment path for extractable brand+model queries, using a trusted manufacturer source and adding only explicitly documented generic facts to an alternate retrieval query; retain the original query and final selection semantics. (2) A small generic quantity/clause-boundary correction that preserves technical designations in retrieval alternates. (3) A later conservative product-intent/uncertainty route restricted to unambiguous service-only or consumable-only queries. Do not repeat deterministic inch/endpoint expansion or generic supplier-token suppression: both have already been rejected by hidden safety gates.', 'decision_impact': 'The strongest new product opportunity is source-backed, additive enrichment of repeated branded model nomenclature, because a model code can resolve endpoint and bore facts that the tender omits. It has external dependency, latency, caching, and source-trust costs, and must never assert LD equivalence or override reranking. If the Planner wants the lowest-risk bounded experiment instead, select the generic designation/quantity parser repair; it is a correctness fix with narrower expected corpus impact. Keep service abstention separate from either retrieval experiment.', 'unresolved': 'Whether external enrichment improves LD candidate recall enough to justify runtime dependency is unmeasured; manufacturer documents establish source-product properties, not a suitable LD substitute. The CRC-corrupt review-pool artifact should be repaired separately, although its intended membership is reconstructable from the other corpus files.', 'sources': [{'url': 'https://www.ivrvalvole.it/media/pdf/schede/IVR_954_956_957.pdf', 'claim': 'Official IVR technical sheet identifies IVR 954/956/957 as full-bore threaded ball valves and distinguishes F/F, M/F, and M/M endpoints; it also provides Russian terminology.', 'quality': 'official', 'confidence': 0.98}, {'url': 'https://valtec.ru/document/Catalog_VALTEC.pdf?69a765ad99bad=', 'claim': 'Official VALTEC catalogue identifies VT.214 as a ball valve with a steel handle and internal-to-internal threaded connection.', 'quality': 'official', 'confidence': 0.95}], 'origin': 'attempt-03-research-first', 'kind': 'research-first'}, {'question': 'What causal mechanisms remain promising for improving real-tender LD matching after the current champion and prior experiments?', 'findings': 'The active production path retrieves with the original query plus at most one canonical alternate, fuses dense/BM25 candidates into a fixed top-20, then reranks against the untouched original query. Canonicalization is therefore retrieval-only and fail-open. In the reconstructed 130-row review set, 53 rows mention ball valves, 50 threaded/inch-style cues, 43 third-party brands (30 IVR), 33 filter/water-treatment rows, and 11 explicit service-action rows. Only 40/130 currently receive a canonical alternate. The catalog contains 15,788 products, including substantial ball-valve and butterfly coverage, but no IVR/VALTEC/TECOFI/БИВАЛ tokens; it has no cartridge or water-treatment products, while its 129 “filter” products are principally грязевики. A confirmed parser defect truncates “Кран БИВАЛ КШТ.11.050.025.ф/ф 50х25 КОФ” to “Кран БИВАЛ К”: the clause-end quantity pattern can recognize embedded “ШТ.” without a required leading token boundary. This is a general parsing error, not a one-off rule. No new evidence supports another branded-model suppression or source-enrichment refinement: three such attempts already increased hidden wrong-NOT_FOUND rate despite retaining original-query retrieval.', 'decision_impact': 'The main uncertainty is whether useful unresolved value is constrained by loss of query evidence during normalization and late fusion, or by genuine catalog-scope/service-consumable requests that should produce uncertainty rather than more retrieval. The Planner should distinguish these mechanisms. Do not select another endpoint/inch, branded-token suppression, or manufacturer-model enrichment variant without new causal evidence; those paths are already tested and unsafe.', 'unresolved': 'The review corpus is unresolved rather than outcome-labeled, so its category counts establish opportunity and scope but not end-to-end uplift. The supplied review-pool gzip remains corrupt; membership is reconstructable from the intact all-rows, labels, and provisional-NOT_FOUND files. It is also unmeasured whether correcting the canonical alternate changes the final top-20, because the original query is retained and may already supply the needed candidate.', 'sources': [], 'evidence_patterns': [{'pattern': 'Narrow additive retrieval normalization has conditional value; semantic expansion is not generally beneficial.', 'supporting_experiments': ['legacy-cycle-3 ACCEPTED: deterministic query canonicalization improved safely.', 'legacy-cycle-4 ACCEPTED: standalone WW expansion improved safely.', 'legacy-cycle-6 REJECTED: flanged-shorthand canonicalization regressed hidden safety.', 'legacy-cycle-9 REJECTED: standard-bore wording expansion was neutral.', 'legacy-cycle-17 REJECTED: installed-electric versus actuator-ready alternate had an unreliable catalog semantic premise.'], 'interpretation': 'The successful causal path is preservation/translation of unambiguous catalog vocabulary, not adding plausible domain semantics. The present parser truncation directly destroys source evidence inside that proven retrieval-only path, so repairing it is materially different from adding another alias.', 'confidence': 0.94}, {'pattern': 'Changes that alter candidate composition or final compatibility selection have repeatedly failed to improve end-to-end utility.', 'supporting_experiments': ['legacy cycles 1-2: broad filtering and compatibility-evidence intervention regressed.', 'legacy-cycle-5 REJECTED: evidence-first reranker rubric regressed blind safety.', 'legacy-cycle-8 REJECTED: deterministic post-rerank compatibility substitution was neutral.', 'legacy-cycle-16 REJECTED: candidate diversification regressed public coverage.', 'legacy-cycle-7 REJECTED: catalog structural representation reduced hidden coverage.'], 'interpretation': 'The evidence does not show that more candidate filtering, compatibility gating, prompt changes, diversification, or catalog rewriting is the current bottleneck. A new decision/abstention layer would need a sharply separable request-intent signal, not generic technical compatibility rules.', 'confidence': 0.91}, {'pattern': 'Branded tender nomenclature is common, but prior genericization and external-fact enrichment were unsafe.', 'supporting_experiments': ['attempt-01 alias_mapping REJECTED: threaded/inch expansion increased hidden wrong-NOT_FOUND rate by 0.04.', 'attempt-02 alias_mapping REJECTED: supplier/model-noise suppression increased hidden wrong-NOT_FOUND rate by 0.04.', 'attempt-03 alias_mapping REJECTED: trusted manufacturer/model facts increased hidden wrong-NOT_FOUND rate by 0.08.'], 'interpretation': 'Opaque brand/model text is a real corpus mismatch, but making it more generic or importing source facts did not establish LD interchangeability and degraded safety. This points to underspecification/equivalence uncertainty rather than a simple lexical-recall deficit.', 'confidence': 0.96}, {'pattern': 'A distinct non-catalog/service class is large enough to compete with more retrieval work.', 'supporting_experiments': ['Real-corpus inspection: 33 review rows are filter/water-treatment related; examples include cartridges, filter media, water-treatment units, and service work.', 'Catalog inspection: zero catalog texts contain cartridge/ЭФГ or water-treatment terms; 129 filter entries are largely грязевики.', 'Real-corpus inspection: 11 review rows explicitly request removal, repair, installation, or maintenance.'], 'interpretation': 'For many rows, better retrieval cannot create a compatible sellable LD product. Yet action words alone are insufficient, because some installation/removal lines mention a product family; any intervention must establish service-only or absent-capability evidence affirmatively.', 'confidence': 0.88}], 'candidate_directions': [{'mechanism_family': 'query_evidence_preservation', 'history_relation': 'REFINEMENT', 'causal_mechanism': 'Repair structural line-item/quantity boundary parsing so a canonical retrieval alternate cannot stop inside an alphanumeric technical designation; retain the raw query, all existing canonical transformations, and final reranking behavior.', 'competing_explanation': 'Because raw-query retrieval remains active, the damaged alternate may not materially affect candidate availability or final selection; the observed defect may be operationally harmless on most rows.', 'falsifier': 'A stratified real-tender retrieval comparison shows that preserving affected designations does not add or improve viable family-consistent candidates in the pre-rerank pool, while public/hidden gates remain flat.', 'information_gain': 'High confidence in correctness and moderate information gain: it isolates whether an established successful mechanism is currently losing evidence through parsing rather than through retrieval or reranking.'}, {'mechanism_family': 'query_variant_evidence_fusion', 'history_relation': 'NEW_LAYER', 'causal_mechanism': 'Represent original and canonical retrieval hits as separate evidence channels through fusion, rather than collapsing each modality to one locally best rank before RRF; reward candidates corroborated by both query forms without removing candidates or changing reranker semantics.', 'competing_explanation': 'The primary limitation may be candidate absence or reranker choice, so preserving alternate-query corroboration may not alter the fixed top-20 meaningfully; candidate-composition changes have previously been risky.', 'falsifier': 'On a real-tender stratification of rows with canonical alternates, variant-aware fusion does not improve family/constraint-consistent candidate presence or rank, or it breaches public/hidden coverage or safety gates.', 'information_gain': 'Moderate-to-high: it tests an untried architectural implication of the accepted canonicalization mechanism while avoiding another semantic expansion or index rebuild.'}, {'mechanism_family': 'catalog_scope_and_request_intent', 'history_relation': 'NEW_LAYER', 'causal_mechanism': 'Use affirmative evidence of service-only procurement or a request category absent from the LD product taxonomy to route toward an uncertain/NOT_FOUND outcome, while allowing lines that name an actual purchasable product to continue through ordinary retrieval.', 'competing_explanation': 'Tender work descriptions can embed an intended product, and catalog lexical fields can be noisy; a router could convert recoverable matches into wrong NOT_FOUND, reproducing prior selection-adjacent regressions.', 'falsifier': 'A manually reviewed non-benchmark sample shows material overlap between the proposed service/absent-category cues and viable LD product requests, or regression gates show increased wrong-NOT_FOUND.', 'information_gain': 'High: it separates genuine catalog noncoverage from retrieval failure in the sizeable consumable, water-treatment, and service portion of the real corpus.'}], 'origin': 'attempt-01-research-first', 'kind': 'research-first'}, {'question': 'What causal mechanisms remain credible after evidence synthesis for Harness v2 attempt 2?', 'findings': 'The current path is raw-query retrieval plus at most one canonical alternate, merged per modality by its single best variant rank, then RRF top-20 and reranking against the untouched raw query. In the reconstructed 130-row review set, 69 mention valves/cranes, 52 have threaded/inch cues, 39 contain third-party brand cues, 33 concern filters/water treatment, and 11 are explicit service actions; only 40 rows receive a canonical alternate. The catalog has 15,788 products with extensive ball-valve (14,428) and butterfly-valve (356) coverage, but no IVR/VALTEC/TECOFI, cartridge, or water-treatment terminology; its 129 filter entries are not cartridge/water-treatment products. A real parser defect is confirmed: an embedded technical-designation substring “КШТ.” is treated as a quantity boundary and reduces one review query to “Кран БИВАЛ К”. This is a generic boundary error, but only one affected review row was observed, so its expected direct corpus value is limited. There is no new evidence for another branded-token suppression, threaded/inch semantic expansion, or manufacturer enrichment refinement: all three evaluated attempts raised hidden wrong-NOT_FOUND rates.', 'decision_impact': 'The main decision is whether unresolved value is primarily lost inside the accepted alternate-query retrieval mechanism, or whether a substantial portion of the corpus is genuinely outside LD’s catalog scope and needs honest uncertainty. Do not infer that more semantic expansion is the bottleneck: repeated branded-query transformations were unsafe. A bounded experiment should discriminate evidence-preservation/fusion from non-catalog intent while retaining raw retrieval and guarding against wrong NOT_FOUND.', 'unresolved': 'The review set is intentionally unresolved, so its class counts show opportunity rather than end-to-end uplift. The raw query remains active, so the parser defect may not affect final candidate availability. The supplied review-pool gzip remains corrupt, although its 130 intended rows are exactly reconstructable from the intact all-row, label, and provisional-NOT_FOUND files.', 'sources': [], 'evidence_patterns': [{'pattern': 'Semantics-preserving retrieval canonicalization is the only repeatedly validated mechanism, while added domain semantics do not reliably improve end-to-end outcomes.', 'supporting_experiments': ['Legacy cycles 3 and 4 were accepted for additive deterministic canonicalization, including standalone WW translation.', 'Legacy cycle 6 flanged-shorthand expansion regressed blind safety; cycle 9 standard-bore expansion was neutral; cycle 17 actuation-state expansion was rejected.'], 'interpretation': 'The supported causal path is preserving or translating unambiguous evidence into catalog vocabulary, not completing underspecified technical meaning. The confirmed embedded-quantity boundary error directly damages that established path, but its observed prevalence is low.', 'confidence': 0.95}, {'pattern': 'Genericizing branded nomenclature or importing manufacturer facts repeatedly increased hidden wrong-NOT_FOUND despite retaining raw-query retrieval.', 'supporting_experiments': ['Attempt 1 threaded/inch expansion: hidden wrong-NOT_FOUND +0.04.', 'Attempt 2 supplier/model-noise suppression: hidden wrong-NOT_FOUND +0.04.', 'Attempt 3 trusted manufacturer/model enrichment: hidden wrong-NOT_FOUND +0.08.'], 'interpretation': 'Third-party model strings identify a recurring corpus class, but the causal bottleneck is not merely lexical noise or absent source-product facts. Foreign-product facts do not establish an appropriate LD equivalent; this mechanism family is locally saturated absent materially new evidence.', 'confidence': 0.97}, {'pattern': 'Interventions that filter, alter candidate composition, or influence final selection have not produced a safe gain.', 'supporting_experiments': ['Legacy cycles 1–2 broad gating/compatibility intervention regressed.', 'Legacy cycle 5 reranker rubric regressed; cycle 8 post-rerank compatibility fallback was neutral.', 'Legacy cycle 7 catalog structural enrichment reduced hidden coverage; cycle 16 candidate diversification reduced public coverage.'], 'interpretation': 'Selection-adjacent changes are not categorically impossible, but they require a separable affirmative signal. Generic compatibility, candidate pruning, prompt tightening, and catalog-derived structure are weakly supported causal levers in this system.', 'confidence': 0.92}, {'pattern': 'The unresolved corpus contains a materially distinct non-catalog or service-like segment.', 'supporting_experiments': ['Review-corpus inspection found 33 filter/water-treatment rows and 11 explicit service-action rows.', 'Catalog inspection found zero cartridge/ЭФГ and water-treatment terms, while its filter products are primarily industrial грязевики.', 'Examples include cartridge filters, mixed-action filter disassembly/repair, and water de-ironing installations.'], 'interpretation': 'For many such requests, broader retrieval cannot create a compatible sellable LD product. However, some service text embeds a concrete product request, so action words or the word “filter” alone are not sufficient grounds for NOT_FOUND.', 'confidence': 0.9}, {'pattern': 'Alternate-query evidence is discarded before cross-modality fusion.', 'supporting_experiments': ['Current HybridRetriever retrieves raw and canonical variants, then _merge_modality_candidates retains only the best per-candidate rank within dense and within BM25 before RRF.', '40 of 130 review rows currently receive a canonical alternate.'], 'interpretation': 'A candidate corroborated by raw and canonical wording receives no extra RRF evidence beyond its stronger hit. This is an untested architectural implication of the accepted canonicalization mechanism, distinct from adding another semantic alias; its benefit remains unmeasured.', 'confidence': 0.88}], 'candidate_directions': [{'mechanism_family': 'query_evidence_preservation', 'history_relation': 'REFINEMENT', 'causal_mechanism': 'Repair structural clause/quantity boundary recognition so canonical retrieval alternates cannot terminate inside an alphanumeric designation, while preserving raw retrieval, existing transformations, and reranking behavior.', 'competing_explanation': 'Raw-query retrieval already provides the required candidate, and the one observed damaged designation may have no material effect on the final top-20.', 'falsifier': 'On a stratified set of affected technical-designation rows, corrected alternates neither improve viable family-consistent candidate presence/rank nor provide an end-to-end real-tender value signal while guardrails remain flat.', 'information_gain': 'Moderate. It isolates a confirmed correctness failure within the one successful mechanism family, but the observed affected population is small and should not be overstated.'}, {'mechanism_family': 'query_variant_evidence_fusion', 'history_relation': 'NEW_LAYER', 'causal_mechanism': 'Preserve raw-query and canonical-query hits as separate retrieval-evidence channels through fusion, rewarding cross-variant corroboration without removing candidates or changing reranker inputs/selection semantics.', 'competing_explanation': 'Canonical alternates may mostly retrieve the same candidates already reached by raw retrieval; the real bottleneck may be catalog absence or reranker choice rather than loss of variant provenance.', 'falsifier': 'Among rows with canonical alternates, variant-aware fusion does not improve viable family/constraint-consistent candidate presence or rank, or it breaches public/hidden safety or coverage gates.', 'information_gain': 'High. It tests whether accepted canonicalization has unrealized value because the current merger discards its second evidence signal, without repeating semantic expansion or catalog rewriting.'}, {'mechanism_family': 'catalog_scope_and_request_intent', 'history_relation': 'NEW_LAYER', 'causal_mechanism': 'Use only affirmative combined evidence of service-only procurement or a requested product category absent from the LD taxonomy to expose uncertain/NOT_FOUND rather than force ordinary product selection; lines containing a purchasable product continue through normal retrieval.', 'competing_explanation': 'Tender work descriptions can describe installation or repair alongside an intended LD product, so an intent route could create wrong NOT_FOUND outcomes and repeat earlier selection-adjacent regressions.', 'falsifier': 'A manually reviewed non-benchmark sample shows substantial overlap between the proposed combined cues and viable LD product requests, or regression gates increase wrong-NOT_FOUND.', 'information_gain': 'High. It directly distinguishes genuine catalog noncoverage from retrieval failure in a large real-tender class and tests the product goal’s uncertainty requirement.'}], 'origin': 'attempt-02-research-first', 'kind': 'research-first'}, {'question': 'What causal mechanisms remain credible for Attempt 3 after inspecting the champion, real-tender corpus, and evaluated experiment history?', 'findings': 'The champion retrieves the raw line plus at most one canonical alternate, collapses raw/canonical hits to the best rank within each modality, RRF-fuses dense and BM25, and gives only the untouched raw line to DeepSeek for final selection. In the reconstructed 130-row review set, 48 are ball-valve requests, 45 contain threaded/inch cues, 43 contain third-party brand/model cues, 33 concern filters/water treatment, and 20 contain work-action wording. The LD CSV has no IVR, VALTEC, cartridge/ЭФГ, or water-treatment terms. Of the 20 action rows, some explicitly name a valve or filter product, so action wording alone is not a safe abstention signal.\n\nThe local, nearby retrieval space is now substantially saturated: endpoint/inch expansion, vendor-token suppression, manufacturer-fact enrichment, quantity-boundary repair, and variant-aware fusion all had neutral or unsafe end-to-end results. The latter two are especially important because code confirms their premises, but their evaluated changes still increased wrong-NOT_FOUND or failed public safety. Evidence supports investigating request granularity and catalog-scope uncertainty rather than another lexical or fusion refinement.', 'decision_impact': 'The central uncertainty is whether unresolved tender value is mostly recoverable product evidence obscured by mixed service/product line items, or honest catalog-scope uncertainty for requests outside LD’s sellable taxonomy. The next experiment should discriminate those explanations while preserving raw retrieval and avoiding a forced MATCHED/NOT_FOUND decision. There is insufficient evidence for another nearby branded-model, endpoint/inch, canonicalization, parser, or query-variant-fusion refinement.', 'unresolved': 'The review pool is unresolved, so category prevalence is not proof of end-to-end uplift. Lexical absence from the catalog is supporting evidence rather than proof of product absence; any scope mechanism needs affirmative taxonomy/category evidence and a fail-open path. The supplied review-pool gzip remains unreadable locally, but its 130 members are exactly reconstructable from the intact full corpus minus the 90 labels and 33 provisional cases.', 'sources': [], 'evidence_patterns': [{'pattern': 'Semantics-preserving retrieval changes have a narrow success boundary; semantic completion and alternate-ranking changes have not safely improved end-to-end outcomes.', 'supporting_experiments': ['Legacy cycles 3–4 accepted additive canonicalization.', 'Legacy cycles 6, 9, and 17 rejected flanged, standard-bore, and actuation semantic expansions.', 'Attempt 1 query_evidence_preservation improved public known-positive hit rate but raised hidden wrong-NOT_FOUND by 0.08.', 'Attempt 2 query_variant_evidence_fusion raised public wrong-NOT_FOUND by 0.04.'], 'interpretation': 'The code confirms that canonical variants are currently collapsed before RRF, and that a quantity-boundary defect exists. But both a repair of that defect and preservation of variant provenance have already been scientifically evaluated without safe end-to-end value. These are not credible nearby repeats absent new causal evidence.', 'confidence': 0.97}, {'pattern': 'Genericizing third-party nomenclature or importing external product facts repeatedly harms abstention safety.', 'supporting_experiments': ['Attempt 1 threaded/inch alias expansion: hidden wrong-NOT_FOUND +0.04.', 'Attempt 2 supplier/model-noise suppression: hidden wrong-NOT_FOUND +0.04.', 'Attempt 3 trusted manufacturer/model enrichment: hidden wrong-NOT_FOUND +0.08.', 'Review corpus: 43 branded/model-like rows; catalog lexical scan: no IVR or VALTEC tokens.'], 'interpretation': 'Branded nomenclature is a real lexical mismatch, but the repeated failure signature indicates that source-product facts and generic wording do not establish an appropriate LD equivalent. This family is locally saturated.', 'confidence': 0.98}, {'pattern': 'Selection-adjacent candidate manipulation is high risk, but catalog scope is a distinct product problem not addressed by retrieval.', 'supporting_experiments': ['Legacy cycles 1–2, 5, 7, 8, and 16 found gating, compatibility prompting, index enrichment, fallback substitution, or diversification neutral or harmful.', 'Review corpus: 33 filter/water-treatment rows; 13 contain cartridge/ЭФГ/sorbent/water-treatment cues without a valve-family cue.', 'Catalog lexical scan: no cartridge/ЭФГ or water-treatment terms.'], 'interpretation': 'Broad filtering or selection rules should not be retried. A narrowly affirmative catalog-scope mechanism is causally different if it reports uncertainty rather than selecting a substitute or asserting catalog absence from weak evidence.', 'confidence': 0.91}, {'pattern': 'Tender lines mix procurement work with product nouns, making line-item granularity a plausible upstream bottleneck.', 'supporting_experiments': ['Review corpus: 20 rows contain installation, removal, disassembly, repair, or maintenance actions.', 'Five action rows also name a valve-family product; examples include installation/removal of ball valves and a line containing a butterfly-valve product.', 'Current canonicalization extracts a textual clause but has no explicit work-versus-product decomposition.'], 'interpretation': 'An action-word NOT_FOUND rule would be unsafe, but separating an explicit purchasable product phrase from surrounding work language could distinguish recoverable product requests from service-only requests. This is materially different from supplier-token suppression.', 'confidence': 0.86}], 'candidate_directions': [{'mechanism_family': 'catalog_scope_uncertainty', 'history_relation': 'NEW_LAYER', 'causal_mechanism': 'Use affirmative, catalog-taxonomy-backed evidence that a requested category is outside LD’s sellable product scope to return an explicit uncertain/no-catalog-evidence outcome, while retaining ordinary retrieval for ambiguous or product-bearing lines. Do not infer absence from a single unmatched token and do not substitute an unrelated LD item.', 'competing_explanation': 'The apparent noncoverage may be catalog synonymy or a retrieval/index representation failure; routing could hide a valid LD product or create wrong NOT_FOUND behavior.', 'falsifier': 'A blinded manual review of a stratified non-benchmark sample finds viable LD products for a material share of rows meeting the proposed combined cues, or regression evaluation increases wrong-NOT_FOUND.', 'information_gain': 'High. It directly tests whether a meaningful part of real-tender difficulty is catalog scope rather than retrieval, while aligning with the product goal’s preference for honest uncertainty.'}, {'mechanism_family': 'line_item_product_decomposition', 'history_relation': 'NEW_MECHANISM', 'causal_mechanism': 'Extract a bounded purchasable-product span from mixed work/service nomenclature and use it only as an additive retrieval representation; retain the complete raw line and leave final compatibility selection unchanged. Service-only spans should not manufacture a product query.', 'competing_explanation': 'Mixed work wording may be useful context, and the apparent product phrase may be too underspecified to improve retrieval; decomposition could repeat unsafe genericization under another name.', 'falsifier': 'On a stratified real-tender sample containing both action and product cues, extracted product spans do not improve family-consistent candidate presence/rank over raw retrieval, or public/hidden guardrails regress.', 'information_gain': 'High. It separates recoverable product mentions embedded in work descriptions from genuinely service-only lines without relying on the already-rejected branded-model transformations.'}, {'mechanism_family': 'uncertainty_preserving_result_contract', 'history_relation': 'NEW_LAYER', 'causal_mechanism': 'Represent insufficient technical evidence separately from a confident product match and expose a useful candidate set or an explicit uncertainty reason when multiple candidates remain plausible, instead of making the final interface binary by default.', 'competing_explanation': 'The current reranker can already select multiple candidates, so the bottleneck may be candidate quality rather than result semantics; extra states may add complexity without changing user utility.', 'falsifier': 'A sampled review workflow shows that the proposed uncertainty state does not improve the ability to distinguish unsupported, underspecified, and viable multi-candidate requests, or it encourages unsupported matches/abstentions under regression gates.', 'information_gain': 'Moderate-to-high. It tests whether measured pipeline failures partly arise from a binary decision contract that cannot faithfully express the product goal, rather than from another retrieval-rank adjustment.'}], 'origin': 'attempt-03-research-first', 'kind': 'research-first'}, {'question': 'What causal mechanisms remain credible for Harness v2 attempt 4 after inspecting the champion, corpus, code, and experiment ledger?', 'findings': 'The champion retrieves the raw query plus at most one canonical alternate, collapses each modality’s raw/alternate hits to the single strongest rank per product, RRF-fuses top candidates, and asks the reranker to return only MATCHED or NOT_FOUND against the untouched raw query. Although up to three candidates can be selected, there is no uncertainty state. The prompt explicitly favors avoiding NOT_FOUND when a candidate is reasonably compatible.\n\nThe intended review set reconstructs to 130 rows when the 90 keyed labels and 33 provisional rows are excluded from all 253 rows. The supervisor digest’s 220-row reconstruction conflicts with the valid keyed-label JSON and README because it reports zero parsed labels; its class counts should not be combined with 130-row research counts until that ingestion contract is corrected. On the reconstructed set, 40 rows receive a canonical alternate; 17 have clear cartridge/media/water-treatment cues and 18 have service-action cues. These include both genuine service/consumable requests and product-bearing work lines, so neither “filter” nor an action verb alone supports abstention. Catalog text contains zero occurrences of cartridge, ЭФГ, Lewatit, Honeywell, IVR, VALTEC, water-treatment, or ion-exchange terminology, while its filter products are predominantly грязевики.\n\nThe local retrieval-normalization space is saturated: prior semantic expansion, branded-query genericization/enrichment, canonical-evidence preservation, variant fusion, and work/product decomposition all produced either no safe gain or increased wrong-NOT_FOUND. No evidence supports another nearby alternate-query or fusion refinement.', 'decision_impact': 'The meaningful unresolved trade-off is whether a large portion of real-tender difficulty is genuine catalog-scope/evidence insufficiency rather than missing retrieval vocabulary. The next experiment should distinguish those explanations without converting product-bearing service lines into NOT_FOUND. Separately, resolve the corpus label-schema mismatch before using the deterministic 220-row reconstructed pool to prioritize mechanisms.', 'unresolved': 'The unresolved corpus has no end-to-end truth labels, so category prevalence is opportunity evidence rather than measured uplift. It is unmeasured whether users benefit more from an explicit uncertain candidate set than from the present forced binary decision. A scope signal must prove both the requested non-sellable category and absence from the LD taxonomy; lexical absence alone is insufficient.', 'sources': [], 'evidence_patterns': [{'pattern': 'Query rewriting and retrieval-evidence refinements have repeatedly improved intermediate retrieval behavior or plausibility without safe end-to-end utility.', 'supporting_experiments': ['Legacy cycles 3–4 accepted narrow additive canonicalization.', 'Legacy cycles 6, 9, and 17 rejected flanged, standard-bore, and actuation-state expansion.', 'Attempt 1 query_evidence_preservation improved public known-positive hit rate but raised hidden wrong-NOT_FOUND by 0.08.', 'Attempt 2 query_variant_evidence_fusion improved several public coverage metrics but raised public wrong-NOT_FOUND by 0.04.', 'Attempt 3 line_item_product_decomposition improved public known-positive hit rate but raised hidden wrong-NOT_FOUND by 0.04.'], 'interpretation': 'The causal bottleneck is unlikely to be another way of producing, preserving, or rewarding a canonical alternate. The raw query remains active, and added alternate evidence has repeatedly changed candidate availability/rank without safely improving the final decision.', 'confidence': 0.97}, {'pattern': 'Genericizing branded nomenclature or importing external manufacturer facts is a repeated unsafe causal family.', 'supporting_experiments': ['Alias-mapping attempt 1: threaded/inch expansion increased hidden wrong-NOT_FOUND by 0.04.', 'Alias-mapping attempt 2: supplier/model-noise suppression increased hidden wrong-NOT_FOUND by 0.04.', 'Alias-mapping attempt 3: trusted manufacturer/model fact enrichment increased hidden wrong-NOT_FOUND by 0.08.', 'Reconstructed review corpus contains many branded/model-bearing rows; catalog text has no IVR, VALTEC, or TECOFI occurrences.'], 'interpretation': 'Brand/model opacity is real, but foreign-product facts do not establish a suitable LD equivalent. Another branded-token, supplier suppression, or runtime enrichment refinement lacks a changed causal premise.', 'confidence': 0.98}, {'pattern': 'Candidate manipulation and final-selection interventions have not safely resolved the main problem.', 'supporting_experiments': ['Legacy cycles 1–2: gating and compatibility intervention regressed.', 'Legacy cycle 5: reranker-rubric change regressed.', 'Legacy cycle 7: catalog structural enrichment reduced hidden coverage.', 'Legacy cycle 8: post-rerank compatibility fallback was neutral.', 'Legacy cycle 16: candidate diversification reduced public coverage.'], 'interpretation': 'A new selection rule should require a sharply separable affirmative signal. Generic compatibility filtering, pruning, prompt tightening, and catalog retrieval rewriting are locally unsupported.', 'confidence': 0.94}, {'pattern': 'The corpus contains an apparent non-catalog/service segment, while the runtime contract cannot express evidence insufficiency separately from catalog absence.', 'supporting_experiments': ['Reconstructed review inspection found clear cartridge/media/water-treatment and service-action rows, including both service-only and product-bearing examples.', 'Catalog lexical inspection found zero cartridge, ЭФГ, ion-exchange, water-treatment, Lewatit, and Honeywell terms; it contains only limited грязевик-style filter coverage.', 'Current MatchResult and reranker JSON permit only MATCHED or NOT_FOUND; reranker instructions prioritize avoiding NOT_FOUND.'], 'interpretation': 'This is a distinct product mechanism from retrieval tuning: users may need an explicit no-catalog-evidence or uncertain-candidate outcome. It must remain fail-open because work descriptions can contain a purchasable valve or filter.', 'confidence': 0.91}], 'candidate_directions': [{'mechanism_family': 'catalog_scope_uncertainty', 'history_relation': 'NEW_LAYER', 'causal_mechanism': 'Use affirmative combined evidence that the requested item is a non-sellable consumable, water-treatment medium/system, or service-only work and that its category is absent from the LD taxonomy, then expose an uncertain/no-catalog-evidence outcome. Preserve ordinary raw retrieval for ambiguous lines and for any line with a purchasable product requirement.', 'competing_explanation': 'Catalog lexical absence may reflect synonymy or incomplete representation, and service wording may describe installation or replacement of a sellable 